IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Immigration Act 1959 (Singapore) -- coming in, staying, losing status and being sent away: s 5 (where to cross),
-- ss 6 to 8 (who may enter; prohibited immigrants), s 9 (entry bans), s 9AA (no-boarding directives), s 10 (permanent
-- residence), ss 11 and 14A (permanent residents abroad and automatic cancellation), s 11A (ceasing to be a citizen),
-- s 12 (endorsing a wife or child), s 14 (cancellation), s 15 and s 11A(6) (remaining unlawfully), ss 32, 33, 33A, 35
-- and 57(3) (removal and arrest), s 36 (returning after removal), ss 39A and 39B (no judicial review, no hearing),
-- s 58 (general penalty). From the Immigration Regulations: reg 6(1) (the 180-day period), reg 12(1) to (1B) (visit
-- passes, including for an exempt prohibited immigrant) and Sixth Schedule items 1 and 2 (entry and re-entry permit fees).
--
-- SEAT: the non-citizen who comes to, stays in or is sent away from Singapore (a visitor, pass-holder, permanent
-- resident or former citizen), and the citizen only where the Act speaks to the citizen at the border.
--
-- Edition: Immigration Act 1959, 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 30 September 2026, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1959.txt; Immigration Regulations (Rg 1), informal consolidation in
-- force from 1 January 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1959-RG1.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 2 definitions beyond those used here; s 5A to 5B (passports, children prevented from leaving,
-- facilities); s 6A (children born in Singapore who are not citizens); Part 2A (visas) beyond s 9C(1); Part 4 (arrival
-- procedure, carriers' passenger information, examination); detention beyond s 35's 14 days; Parts 5A and 5B; the
-- classes of pass other than the visit pass; the officers' powers in Part 6. The offences a person meets when housing,
-- employing or marrying a foreigner, and false information, are in imm-offences.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled
-- on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Immigration Act 1959 -- entering and staying`

-- What a court can sentence me to. One shape for every penalty clause encoded here.
--   prison is mandatory      -- "shall ... be punished with imprisonment" (not "liable to")
--   least months in prison   -- a presumptive or stated minimum term; 0 where the text states none
--   most months in prison    -- the maximum term; 0 where imprisonment is not available
--   most dollars of fine     -- the maximum ordinary fine; 0 where none
--   caning is mandatory      -- "shall also be punished with caning"
--   least strokes of the cane -- the stated minimum number of strokes; 0 where none is stated
--   most dollars of fine in lieu of caning -- where the person "is not punishable with caning" under s 325(1)(a) or (b)
--                                            of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010
DECLARE Sentence HAS
    `prison is mandatory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `least months in prison` IS A NUMBER
    `most months in prison` IS A NUMBER
    `most dollars of fine` IS A NUMBER
    `caning is mandatory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `least strokes of the cane` IS A NUMBER
    `most dollars of fine in lieu of caning` IS A NUMBER

§§ `58 -- general penalty`

-- s 58: "Any person guilty of an offence under this Act for which no special penalty is provided shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both."
GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for an offence with no special penalty` MEANS
    Sentence OF FALSE, 0, 6, 2000, FALSE, 0, 0

§§ `5 -- entering and leaving only at authorised places`

-- s 5(2): a person "must not, unless compelled by accident or other reasonable cause, enter or attempt to enter
-- Singapore except at an authorised landing place, airport, train checkpoint or point of entry"; s 5(4) the same for
-- leaving. s 5(5): an offence, with no special penalty, so s 58. "A person" -- a citizen too.
-- Authorised place: one the Minister has declared by Gazette notification under s 5(1) or (3) -- asked as a fact.
GIVEN `I crossed at an authorised place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was compelled by accident or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by entering or leaving where I did` IF
        NOT `I crossed at an authorised place`
    AND NOT `I was compelled by accident or other reasonable cause`

§§ `6, 7, 8(2) -- may I enter`

-- s 7(1): "A citizen of Singapore is entitled to enter Singapore without having obtained a permit or pass". (2): the
-- burden of proving citizenship lies on the person.
-- s 6(1): a non-citizen "must not enter or attempt to enter Singapore unless" (a) holding a valid entry or re-entry
-- permit; (b) "his or her name is endorsed upon a valid entry permit or re-entry permit in accordance with section 12,
-- and he or she is in the company of the holder"; (c) holding a valid pass; or (d) exempted by an order under s 56.
-- s 8(2), "Subject to any exemption granted under section 56": (a) a prohibited immigrant in class (o) (banned by a
-- s 9 order) "must not enter Singapore"; (b) any other prohibited immigrant must not enter "unless he or she is in
-- possession of a valid pass in that behalf issuable to a prohibited immigrant under the regulations".
-- Prohibited immigrant: worked out from facts in `Am I a prohibited immigrant` below; here it is given.
DECLARE `My papers` HAS
    `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a valid entry permit or re-entry permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my name is endorsed on a valid permit and I am with its holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a valid pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am exempted by an order under section 56` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a prohibited immigrant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am banned by an order under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my pass is one issuable to a prohibited immigrant` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Footing for entry` IS ONE OF
    `by right, as a citizen`
    `on my permit or pass`
    `exempted by an order under section 56`
    `I may not enter`

GIVEN `my papers` IS A `My papers`
GIVETH A `Footing for entry`
`May I enter Singapore` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `my papers`'s `I am a citizen of Singapore`                 THEN `by right, as a citizen`
        IF `my papers`'s `I am exempted by an order under section 56` THEN `exempted by an order under section 56`
        IF `my papers`'s `I am a prohibited immigrant`
            THEN IF     NOT `my papers`'s `I am banned by an order under section 9`
                    AND `my papers`'s `I hold a valid pass`
                    AND `my papers`'s `my pass is one issuable to a prohibited immigrant`
                 THEN `on my permit or pass`
                 ELSE `I may not enter`
        IF     `my papers`'s `I hold a valid entry permit or re-entry permit`
            OR `my papers`'s `my name is endorsed on a valid permit and I am with its holder`
            OR `my papers`'s `I hold a valid pass`
                                                                     THEN `on my permit or pass`
        OTHERWISE `I may not enter`

-- s 6(3)(a): entering in breach of s 6(1) -- "shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months and shall also be punished with caning with not less than 3 strokes, or where by virtue of
-- section 325(1)(a) or (b) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 he or she is not punishable with caning, he or she
-- shall, in lieu of caning, be punished with a fine not exceeding $6,000".
-- Whether I am punishable with caning is a borrowed term (Criminal Procedure Code 2010), asked as a fact.
GIVEN `I am punishable with caning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for entering without a permit or pass` MEANS
    IF `I am punishable with caning`
    THEN Sentence OF TRUE, 0, 6, 0, TRUE, 3, 0
    ELSE Sentence OF TRUE, 0, 6, 0, FALSE, 0, 6000

§§ `8 -- prohibited immigrants`

-- s 8(1): a non-citizen "who is a member of any of the prohibited classes as defined in subsection (3) or who, in the
-- opinion of the Controller, is a member of any of the prohibited classes, is a prohibited immigrant".
-- (4): "The burden of proof that any person seeking to enter Singapore is not a prohibited immigrant shall lie upon
-- that person."
-- s 8(3) classes, glossed:
--   (a) cannot show means of support for self and dependants or definite employment, or likely to become a charge on
--       the public;  (b) a contagious or infectious disease dangerous to the community;  (ba) "suffering from Acquired
--       Immune Deficiency Syndrome or infected with the Human Immunodeficiency Virus";  (c) refusing a s 29(1)
--       examination;  (d) see `Does my conviction make me a prohibited immigrant`;  (e) a prostitute, or living on or
--       receiving its proceeds;  (f) procuring prostitutes;  (g) "vagrants or habitual beggars";  (h) entry unlawful;
--   (i) advocating violent overthrow, or "disbelieves in or is opposed to established government", or advocating
--       assassination or unlawful destruction of property;  (j) member of an organisation teaching those things;
--   (k) considered undesirable by the Minister on information received;  (l) removed by another country and considered
--       undesirable by the Controller;  (m) lacking valid, or holding forged, travel documents;  (n) "the family and
--       dependants of a prohibited immigrant";  (o) prohibited by a s 9 order.
DECLARE `Prohibited class` IS ONE OF
    `(a) unable to show means of support`
    `(b) a dangerous contagious or infectious disease`
    `(ba) AIDS or HIV infection`
    `(c) refused a medical examination`
    `(d) an unpardoned prison sentence and deemed undesirable`
    `(e) prostitution`
    `(f) procuring prostitutes`
    `(g) a vagrant or habitual beggar`
    `(h) entry was unlawful`
    `(i) opposed to established government`
    `(j) in an organisation opposed to established government`
    `(k) considered undesirable by the Minister`
    `(l) removed elsewhere and considered undesirable`
    `(m) without valid travel documents`
    `(n) family or dependant of a prohibited immigrant`
    `(o) banned by an order under section 9`

GIVEN `the classes I am in` IS A LIST OF `Prohibited class`
      `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Controller is of the opinion that I am in a prohibited class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a prohibited immigrant` IF
        NOT `I am a citizen of Singapore`
    AND (   NOT null `the classes I am in`
         OR `the Controller is of the opinion that I am in a prohibited class`)

-- s 8(3)(d): a person who "(i) has been convicted in any country of an offence for which a sentence of imprisonment
-- has been passed for any term; (ii) has not received a free pardon; and (iii) by reason of the circumstances connected
-- with that conviction is deemed by the Controller to be an undesirable immigrant". A fine alone does not count.
GIVEN `a sentence of imprisonment was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Controller deems me undesirable because of the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my conviction make me a prohibited immigrant` IF
        `a sentence of imprisonment was passed`
    AND NOT `I received a free pardon`
    AND `the Controller deems me undesirable because of the circumstances`

-- Regulations, reg 12(1): a visit pass may be issued "to any person other than a prohibited immigrant who satisfies
-- the Controller that he wishes to enter Singapore -- (a) on a social, business or professional visit; (b) as a
-- tourist; or (c) for the purposes of seeking employment or being employed in Singapore". (1A): "Despite paragraph
-- (1), the Controller may issue a visit pass to a prohibited immigrant referred to in section 8(3)(ba) of the Act (in
-- these Regulations called an exempt prohibited immigrant)" for the same purposes. (1B): such a pass's first validity
-- period "must not exceed 90 days".
-- Whether reg 12(1A) reaches a person in class (ba) who is ALSO in another class is not said: the text names the
-- person "referred to in section 8(3)(ba)" and does not say "only". That case is returned as not covered.
DECLARE `Visit pass outlook` IS ONE OF
    `may be issued, if the Controller is satisfied of my purpose`
    `may be issued to me as an exempt prohibited immigrant, first valid for at most 90 days`
    `cannot be issued to me`
    `not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN `the classes I am in` IS A LIST OF `Prohibited class`
      `my purpose is a visit, tourism or seeking or taking employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Visit pass outlook`
`Can I be issued a visit pass` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `my purpose is a visit, tourism or seeking or taking employment` THEN `cannot be issued to me`
        IF null `the classes I am in` THEN `may be issued, if the Controller is satisfied of my purpose`
        IF all (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS `(ba) AIDS or HIV infection`) `the classes I am in`
            THEN `may be issued to me as an exempt prohibited immigrant, first valid for at most 90 days`
        IF any (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS `(ba) AIDS or HIV infection`) `the classes I am in`
            THEN `not covered by this encoding`
        OTHERWISE `cannot be issued to me`

§§ `9 -- entry bans`

-- s 9(1)(a): the Minister may by order prohibit or limit entry "in the interests of public security or public health,
-- or by reason of any economic, industrial, social, educational or other conditions in Singapore". (1A): "No order made
-- under subsection (1)(a), except an order made in the interests of public security or public health, applies to any
-- person who is outside Singapore at the time when the order is made and who is in possession of a valid re-entry
-- permit or pass lawfully issued to him or her." (2): no order applies to a citizen.
-- (5): arriving, entering or remaining in breach -- "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum term of not less than
-- 2 years and not more than 4 years and shall also be liable to a fine not exceeding $6,000".
DECLARE `My position under a ban` HAS
    `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order is for public security or public health` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was outside Singapore when the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a valid re-entry permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position under a ban`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the entry ban apply to me` IF
        NOT `my position`'s `I am a citizen of Singapore`
    AND (   `my position`'s `the order is for public security or public health`
         OR NOT (    `my position`'s `I was outside Singapore when the order was made`
                 AND `my position`'s `I hold a valid re-entry permit or pass`))

GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for breaching an entry ban` MEANS
    Sentence OF TRUE, 24, 48, 6000, FALSE, 0, 0

§§ `9AA -- no-boarding directives`

-- s 9AA(1): the Controller may direct that a person must not board an in-bound conveyance if (a) a prohibited
-- immigrant; (b) banned by a s 9(1)(a)(i) order; (c) in a class limited by a s 9(1)(a)(ii) order; or (d) the Controller
-- is satisfied that the person poses a safety or health risk, that the person's presence "would be undesirable", or
-- that the person "would not be issued a permit or pass".
-- (2): "must not" issue (a) against a citizen; (b) on the "undesirable" ground against a person holding a valid permit
-- or pass; (c) on the "would not be issued" ground against a person boarding to transit.
-- (3): on grounds (b) or (c), against a person transiting, "only if the order mentioned in that provision prohibits or
-- limits arrival in Singapore".
-- (6): the Controller "is not required to serve the no-boarding directive on the subject person, or otherwise inform
-- the subject person".
DECLARE `No-boarding ground` IS ONE OF
    `I am a prohibited immigrant`
    `an order bans my arrival or entry`
    `an order limits a class I belong to`
    `the Controller is satisfied I pose a risk to safety or health`
    `the Controller is satisfied my presence would be undesirable`
    `the Controller is satisfied I would not be issued a permit or pass`

DECLARE `My boarding` HAS
    `the ground` IS A `No-boarding ground`
    `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a valid permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am only transiting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order prohibits or limits arrival` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my boarding` IS A `My boarding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be directed not to board` IF
        NOT `my boarding`'s `I am a citizen of Singapore`
    AND CONSIDER `my boarding`'s `the ground`
        WHEN `the Controller is satisfied my presence would be undesirable`
            THEN NOT `my boarding`'s `I hold a valid permit or pass`
        WHEN `the Controller is satisfied I would not be issued a permit or pass`
            THEN NOT `my boarding`'s `I am only transiting`
        WHEN `an order bans my arrival or entry`
            THEN NOT `my boarding`'s `I am only transiting` OR `my boarding`'s `the order prohibits or limits arrival`
        WHEN `an order limits a class I belong to`
            THEN NOT `my boarding`'s `I am only transiting` OR `my boarding`'s `the order prohibits or limits arrival`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be told of a no-boarding directive against me` IF FALSE

§§ `10 -- permanent residence`

-- s 10(1): "A non-citizen who wishes to be a permanent resident of Singapore must apply for an entry permit in such form
-- and manner as the Controller requires." (2): "Upon an application ... and on payment of the prescribed fee, the
-- Controller may issue to the applicant an entry permit". Permanent resident (s 2): "the holder of a valid entry permit".
-- No qualifying period and no class of applicant (a citizen's spouse included) is named anywhere in the Act: the grant
-- is discretionary for everyone.
-- Sixth Schedule item 1: "(a) application for each entry permit $100; (b) issuance of each entry permit $20".
DECLARE `Footing for permanent residence` IS ONE OF
    `not needed: I am a citizen`
    `not yet open: I have not applied in the required form and paid the fee`
    `at the Controller's discretion`

GIVEN `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am married to a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I applied in the form the Controller requires and paid the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Footing for permanent residence`
`On what footing can I be made a permanent resident` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am a citizen of Singapore` THEN `not needed: I am a citizen`
        IF NOT `I applied in the form the Controller requires and paid the fee`
            THEN `not yet open: I have not applied in the required form and paid the fee`
        -- `I am married to a citizen` is asked because applicants ask it; s 10 gives it no weight.
        OTHERWISE `at the Controller's discretion`

GIVEN `the permit is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What do I pay in fees for an entry permit` MEANS
    IF `the permit is issued` THEN 100 PLUS 20 ELSE 100

§§ `11, 11AA, 14A -- permanent residents abroad`

-- s 11(1A): "a permanent resident of Singapore who is outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit must apply for
-- a re-entry permit within the prescribed period". Reg 6(1): "the prescribed period is 180 days".
-- (1C): the duty "continues even if the permanent resident re-enters Singapore under a pass during the prescribed
-- period". (1E)(b): the first day is "the date on which the permanent resident is first outside Singapore without a
-- valid re-entry permit". (1F): the first and last days include a Sunday or public holiday.
-- (1D): (1A) does not apply if the resident "has applied for a re-entry permit before the first day" and "the
-- application is pending on that day, or is rejected on or after that day".
-- s 14A(1): the entry permit "is cancelled" if (a) the person does not comply with s 11(1A); (b) applies in time and
-- the Controller rejects the application; or (c) is within s 11(1D) and the Controller rejects it. (2): it takes
-- effect (a) "on the date immediately after the last day of the prescribed period" or (b), (c) on the date immediately
-- after the rejection.
-- s 11(2A): "the Controller may refuse to issue a re-entry permit or a pass to a permanent resident".
--
-- Counting: the first day is day 1 of the 180, so the last day is the first day plus 179 (an inference from (1E) and
-- (1F); the Act does not spell out the count).
GIVEN `the first day I was outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can apply for a re-entry permit` MEANS
    `the first day I was outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit` PLUS 179

GIVEN `the first day I was outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is my entry permit cancelled if I do not apply` MEANS
    `the first day I was outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit` PLUS 180

DECLARE `My time abroad` HAS
    `I am outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I applied before the first day and it was pending then or rejected on or after it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I applied within the 180 days` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my application was rejected` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my time abroad` IS A `My time abroad`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my permanent residence cancelled automatically` IF
        `my time abroad`'s `I am outside Singapore without a valid re-entry permit`
    AND BRANCH
            IF `my time abroad`'s `I applied before the first day and it was pending then or rejected on or after it`
                THEN `my time abroad`'s `my application was rejected`                       -- s 14A(1)(c)
            IF NOT `my time abroad`'s `I applied within the 180 days` THEN TRUE              -- s 14A(1)(a)
            OTHERWISE `my time abroad`'s `my application was rejected`                       -- s 14A(1)(b)

-- The s 11(1A) duty as a regulative rule. Time is counted in days after the first day (day 0), so the 180th day is
-- day 179. Missing it is not an offence: the consequence is s 14A(1)(a), automatic cancellation.
DECLARE `Party abroad` IS ONE OF `the permanent resident`
DECLARE `Act abroad` IS ONE OF `apply for a re-entry permit`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party abroad` `Act abroad`
`Must I apply for a re-entry permit while abroad` MEANS
    PARTY `the permanent resident`
    MUST  `apply for a re-entry permit`
    WITHIN 179
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the permanent resident`

-- Sixth Schedule item 2(a): "issuance of re-entry permit $10 for every year of the validity period of the re-entry
-- permit, or part thereof".
GIVEN `months of validity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What does a re-entry permit cost me` MEANS
    10 TIMES CEILING (`months of validity` DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `11A -- ceasing to be a citizen while in Singapore`

-- s 11A(1): a person in Singapore who ceases to be a citizen "must not remain in Singapore for more than 24 hours after
-- the date on which the person ceases to be a citizen of Singapore unless the person has been issued with a permit or a
-- pass". (4): a person who applies before those 24 hours expire "(a) may remain in Singapore pending the determination"
-- and "(b) ... must not remain in Singapore for more than 24 hours after being informed that the person's application
-- ... has been rejected". The penalty, s 11A(6), is the same as for s 15: see `What can I be sentenced to for
-- remaining unlawfully`.
-- "24 hours after the date": counted here in hours from the time citizenship ended (an inference; the text anchors on
-- the date).
DECLARE `My loss of citizenship` HAS
    `hours since I ceased to be a citizen` IS A NUMBER
    `I hold a permit or pass to remain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I applied within the 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my application was rejected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours since I was told of the rejection` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `my case` IS A `My loss of citizenship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I remain in Singapore after ceasing to be a citizen` IF
    BRANCH
        IF `my case`'s `I hold a permit or pass to remain` THEN TRUE
        IF `my case`'s `I applied within the 24 hours`
            THEN NOT `my case`'s `my application was rejected`
                 OR `my case`'s `hours since I was told of the rejection` AT MOST 24
        OTHERWISE `my case`'s `hours since I ceased to be a citizen` AT MOST 24

§§ `12 -- endorsing a wife or child`

-- s 12: the Controller may, on application by the holder or applicant, "endorse upon the permit, pass or certificate
-- issued to that person the name or names of the wife or child of that person". s 6(1)(b): a person so endorsed may
-- enter "in the company of the holder". The text names a wife, not a husband or a spouse.
DECLARE `My relative` IS ONE OF
    `my wife`
    `my husband`
    `my child`
    `my parent`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A `My relative`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my relative be endorsed on my permit, pass or certificate` IF
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `my wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14 -- cancellation of my permit or certificate`

-- s 14(1): if the holder "seeks to enter Singapore accompanied by any child whose name is not endorsed upon that
-- permit" and who is not otherwise entitled, "the Controller may cancel the permit".
-- (2): on arrival, if "the Controller is satisfied" the permit was issued on "false representation or concealment of a
-- material fact", the Controller may cancel. (3): if "the Controller is satisfied that the holder ... is a prohibited
-- immigrant, the Controller must cancel". (4): if the Controller is satisfied that (a) a material statement was false
-- or misleading, (b) the person is a prohibited immigrant, or (c) the holder contravened the Act, the regulations or a
-- condition, the Controller "may cancel" and "may declare at any time after the date of the entry ... that the presence
-- of that person in Singapore is unlawful". (5): cancelling a re-entry permit for breach of its condition lets the
-- Controller cancel the entry permit too, "whether or not that person has contravened any condition of the entry
-- permit". (5A): for a cancellation under (2), (3), (4) or (5), or a declaration, the Controller "must give notice".
DECLARE `Cancellation ground` IS ONE OF
    `I am a prohibited immigrant`
    `my application had a false or misleading material statement`
    `I contravened the Act, the regulations or a condition`
    `I broke a condition of my re-entry permit, and my entry permit is at stake`
    `I arrived with a child not endorsed on my permit`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Cancellation outlook` IS ONE OF
    `must be cancelled, if the Controller is satisfied of the ground`
    `may be cancelled, if the Controller is satisfied of the ground`
    `may be cancelled`
    `cannot be cancelled under section 14`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Cancellation ground`
GIVETH A `Cancellation outlook`
`Can my permit be cancelled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `I am a prohibited immigrant` THEN `must be cancelled, if the Controller is satisfied of the ground`
    WHEN `my application had a false or misleading material statement`
        THEN `may be cancelled, if the Controller is satisfied of the ground`
    WHEN `I contravened the Act, the regulations or a condition`
        THEN `may be cancelled, if the Controller is satisfied of the ground`
    WHEN `I broke a condition of my re-entry permit, and my entry permit is at stake`
        THEN `may be cancelled, if the Controller is satisfied of the ground`
    WHEN `I arrived with a child not endorsed on my permit` THEN `may be cancelled`
    OTHERWISE `cannot be cancelled under section 14`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Cancellation ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given notice of the cancellation` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `I arrived with a child not endorsed on my permit` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `15, 11A(6) -- remaining unlawfully`

-- s 15(1): a person "must not remain in Singapore after the cancellation of any permit or certificate, or after the
-- making of a declaration under section 14(4) or after the expiration or notification ... of the cancellation of any
-- pass" unless otherwise entitled. (3): contravening it "without reasonable cause" is an offence --
--   (a) "for a period not exceeding 90 days": "a fine not exceeding $4,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding
--       6 months or ... both";
--   (b) "for a period exceeding 90 days": "shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding
--       6 months and shall also be punished with caning with not less than 3 strokes", or a fine up to $6,000 in lieu of
--       caning where the person is not punishable with caning.
-- s 11A(6) is the same for a former citizen who stays beyond the 24 hours.
GIVEN `days I remained unlawfully` IS A NUMBER
      `I had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of remaining unlawfully` IF
    `days I remained unlawfully` GREATER THAN 0 AND NOT `I had reasonable cause`

GIVEN `days I remained unlawfully` IS A NUMBER
      `I am punishable with caning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for remaining unlawfully` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `days I remained unlawfully` AT MOST 90 THEN Sentence OF FALSE, 0, 6, 4000, FALSE, 0, 0
        IF `I am punishable with caning`         THEN Sentence OF TRUE,  0, 6, 0,    TRUE,  3, 0
        OTHERWISE                                     Sentence OF TRUE,  0, 6, 0,    FALSE, 0, 6000

§§ `32, 33, 33A, 35, 57(3) -- removal`

-- s 32(1): a person "convicted of an offence under section 5, 6, 8 or 9 is liable to be removed". (2): "A citizen of
-- Singapore convicted of an offence under section 5 must not be ordered to be removed".
-- s 33(1): a person whose presence is unlawful by reason of s 15 is liable to be removed "whether or not any
-- proceedings are taken". (5): "any permit, pass or certificate ... is cancelled on the date of the order". (6): the
-- Controller need not "assign any reason for the making of any order of removal ... which he or she considers it to be
-- against the public interest to do so".
-- s 33A(1): a former citizen within s 11A(1) may be ordered removed "if the Controller is satisfied that" the person is
-- a prohibited immigrant or the person's presence "is undesirable or would be prejudicial to public security".
-- s 36(3): a person convicted of returning after removal is liable to be removed.
-- s 57(3): a person "unlawfully entering or re-entering ... or unlawfully remaining" is liable to be removed whether or
-- not proceedings are taken.
-- s 35: a person reasonably believed liable to removal may be arrested without warrant "and may be detained ... for a
-- period not exceeding 14 days pending a decision".
-- A citizen is never removable under these provisions: s 32(2) says so for s 5, and ss 6, 8, 9, 15, 33A and 36 each
-- reach only non-citizens, removed persons or former citizens (an inference from the text of each).
DECLARE `Removal ground` IS ONE OF
    `I was convicted under section 5, 6, 8 or 9`
    `I am unlawfully in Singapore under section 15`
    `I entered or remained unlawfully (section 57(3))`
    `I was convicted of returning after removal`
    `I am a former citizen the Controller is satisfied is a prohibited immigrant or undesirable`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Removal ground`
      `I am a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be ordered to be removed from Singapore` IF
        NOT `I am a citizen of Singapore`
    AND CONSIDER `the ground`
        WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days can I be held before it is decided whether to remove me` MEANS 14

GIVEN `the Controller considers giving reasons against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given the reason for my removal order` IF
    NOT `the Controller considers giving reasons against the public interest`

§§ `36 -- coming back after removal`

-- s 36(1): a person "removed from or otherwise lawfully sent out of Singapore must not enter or reside in Singapore
-- without the prior written permission of the Controller". (2): "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum term of not
-- less than one year and not more than 3 years and shall also be liable to a fine not exceeding $6,000".
GIVEN `I was removed or lawfully sent out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have the Controller's prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by coming back` IF
    `I was removed or lawfully sent out` AND NOT `I have the Controller's prior written permission`

GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for coming back after removal` MEANS
    Sentence OF TRUE, 12, 36, 6000, FALSE, 0, 0

§§ `39A, 39B -- no judicial review, no hearing`

-- s 39A(1): "There shall be no judicial review in any court of any act done or decision made by the Minister or the
-- Controller under any provision of this Act except in regard to any question relating to compliance with any
-- procedural requirement of this Act or the regulations governing that act or decision." (2): judicial review
-- includes quashing, mandatory and prohibiting orders, declarations, injunctions, "an Order for Review of Detention" and
-- "any other suit or action".
-- s 39B: the Controller or Minister "is not required to give any person who may be affected by the decision an
-- opportunity to be heard".
DECLARE `Review ground` IS ONE OF
    `a procedural requirement of the Act or regulations was not complied with`
    `I was not heard`
    `the decision was irrational`
    `the decision was an error of law`
    `my detention is unlawful`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Review ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take the decision to court on this ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `a procedural requirement of the Act or regulations was not complied with` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be heard before a decision about me` IF FALSE
